$''
$'  No lab, no club, no budget: YouTube (BPS.space did most of the'
$'  teaching) and a lot of launches that didn\'t go to plan. I started by'
$'  taking fireworks apart and mounting them in cardboard tubes. The first'
$'  ones exploded; after enough iterations they flew.'
$''
$'  \e[38;2;255;106;46m▸\e[0m Home-mixed solid propellant, and a static fire on a kitchen scale'
$'    to read thrust.'
$'  \e[38;2;255;106;46m▸\e[0m An Arduino flight computer reading an accelerometer and driving'
$'    servos.'
$'  \e[38;2;255;106;46m▸\e[0m Parachute recovery, and cameras on board to film each flight.'
$'  \e[38;2;255;106;46m▸\e[0m Eleven rockets built. One pad fire. One flew in a corkscrew. I'
$'    kept every clip.'
$''
$'  \e[2mfilm\e[0m  Foguete 7/2023, the documentary: https://youtu.be/FnTpVjeVxYo'
$''
$'@a8 t'
$'  \e[2mGold at the 1st National AI Olympiad (ONIA), 2025.\e[0m'
